{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"83e0cc78-c7a2-4790-8104-34584beb86a4","snapshotMessageId":"dccae15b-4603-4f63-9c55-47c6508f06d9","trackingPath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-greg-code-spideryarn2/968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920/scratchpad/fb2f-msg2.txt","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-09-08T08:48:32.428Z","realParentDir":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-greg-code-spideryarn2/968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920/scratchpad"},"timestamp":"2026-09-08T08:48:32.429Z"}
{"parentUuid":"06d2657d-d072-486f-8957-10a7bcb58a11","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeqgZgTaSDb1Gshm2FjYQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fm3JpGgmYHoquA4LSHd1bz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-greg-code-spideryarn2/968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920/scratchpad/fb2f-msg2.txt","content":"GPT Sol's four findings on the guard, two of them mine to fix\n\nThe plan review came back \"build it with changes\", and independently found the\nautofocus problem the browser had already found — so the .mode-band:focus-within\narm was wrong twice over.\n\nTwo were real errors:\n\n- The specificity arithmetic. I called .dock:focus-within (0,3,0); it is\n  (0,2,0), and (0,3,0) is the whole old selector. So the plain spelling raised\n  the guard to (0,4,0) and the transition rule to (0,5,0) while both comments\n  claimed nothing had moved. :where(.reader.band-covers) .mode-band contributes\n  zero and puts both back exactly where they were. Nothing competes either way\n  — what was broken was the comment, which in this file is the record.\n- \"Every band scroller sets overscroll-behavior: contain\" is false.\n  .gloss-list, .srch-saved, .srch-hits and .quotes-list have none. Several is\n  enough for the safety argument and is what it now says.\n\nOne killed an assertion: the test counted parentheses to prove \"one :has()\",\nwhich proves nothing about specificity and would have rejected the :where()\nfix. A test that fails the right answer is worse than no test. It asserts the\nexact selector now.\n\nOne is deferred and written down: the install hint copies one of the guard's\nsix arms and always has, so the dock can be home while the hint is still\ntranslated away. Sol's fix — an inherited --install-hint-transform beside\n--dock-bottom — is right and is not this report.\n\nStill unverified: npm test, npm run typecheck, and a Sol review of the built\ndiff. And the browser tables were measured against the plain spelling, not\n:where(); the two match identically per spec, which is not the same as having\nwatched it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QEYnhykqEyfPtxrQU6GC23\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":214733,"output_tokens":788,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":788,"cache_read_input_tokens":214733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeqgZfDQzemQDv7dv9ZGb","type":"assistant","uuid":"83e0cc78-c7a2-4790-8104-34584beb86a4","timestamp":"2026-09-08T08:48:32.403Z","effort":"high","session_id":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape","sessionId":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"worktree-fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape"}
