{"parentUuid":"8f403b68-0ab4-4470-a1c6-7ba64aca0c78","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14781737 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3883f1b-c018-44d5-9fa7-6bc3026a25f8","timestamp":"2026-09-08T08:49:09.566Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14781737 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape","sessionId":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"worktree-fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape"}
{"parentUuid":"d3883f1b-c018-44d5-9fa7-6bc3026a25f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeqgdVhnE8pVRrL2Upceb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sol's plan review arrived after I'd paused. Reading and applying it costs the box nothing, so I did that rather than let it sit — now genuinely idle until ~12:36.\n\n**Verdict: \"build it with changes.\"** It confirmed the diagnosis against `layout.ts` and `Reader.tsx` — `.reader.band-covers .mode-band` is true exactly when the band covers the prose, including the `?spine=0` (688px) and `?text=0` cases — and named commit `089269a4` as the one that moved the boundary. It also reached the autofocus finding independently, so the `:focus-within` arm was rejected twice over.\n\n**Two findings were real errors of mine:**\n\n- **The specificity arithmetic was wrong.** I called `.dock:focus-within` (0,3,0); it's (0,2,0) — (0,3,0) is the whole old selector. So my spelling actually raised the guard to (0,4,0) and the transition rule to (0,5,0), while both comments claimed nothing had moved. `:where(.reader.band-covers) .mode-band` contributes zero and puts both back exactly where they were. Nothing competes either way; what was broken was the comment, which in that file is the record.\n- **\"Every band scroller sets `overscroll-behavior: contain`\" is false.** I checked: `.gloss-list`, `.srch-saved`, `.srch-hits` and `.quotes-list` have none. \"Several\" carries the safety argument fine, and that's what it says now.\n\n**One killed an assertion in my test** — it counted parentheses to prove \"one `:has()`\", which proves nothing about specificity and would have *rejected* the `:where()` fix. A test that fails the right answer is worse than no test; it asserts the exact selector now.\n\n**One I deferred rather than took.** The install hint copies one of the guard's six arms and always has, so the dock can be home while the hint is still translated off-screen. Sol's fix — an inherited `--install-hint-transform` set beside `--dock-bottom` — is right, and it's an unrequested behaviour change in six untested states riding on a one-line bug fix. Written up under § What was left alone.\n\nOne thing I want to flag rather than bury: **the browser tables were measured against the plain spelling, not `:where()`.** Per spec they match identically, but that's a claim from the spec, not something I watched. The wake-up re-runs both scripts before anything lands.\n\nStill unverified: `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, and a Sol review of the built diff. Nothing on `dev`, Sentry issue still open. HEAD `1c494dc1`, pushed."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":217946,"output_tokens":864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":217946,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CeqgdUc49zCT8MTPateVS","type":"assistant","uuid":"2db132e7-c1cb-4850-b79e-34a55c7cdda3","timestamp":"2026-09-08T08:49:23.017Z","effort":"high","session_id":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape","sessionId":"968beaba-352a-489f-a202-5e1c87403920","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"worktree-fb2f-dock-always-visible-landscape"}
